    "q-163156": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163156",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the function $f(x,y)$ and the region $D$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=6xy,\\,D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 4x\\}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that the volume of the solid enclosed between the surface $z=f(x,y)$ and the $xy$-plane over the region $D$ equals the volume of the right cylinder with base $D$ and height $f(a,b).$ Find $a$ given that $b=2.$",
      "worked_solution": "According to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=f(a,b)\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral on the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}(6xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4x}6xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[3x{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}48{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[12{x}^{4}]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4x}\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[y]_{y=0}^{y=4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we are told that $b=2.$ So, our initial equation simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =f(a,2)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 12 & =(6a\\cdot 2)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 12 & =24a \\\\ a & =\\frac{12}{24} \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $(\\frac{1}{2},2)\\in D.$ Therefore, the answer is $a=\\frac{1}{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
